  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/mugilogobius_rexi_en/",
      "html": "<p>This small, yellow goby is a free swimming species, in contrast to most of the other gobies. Maximum length is about 4-5 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/mugilogobius_rexi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species is restricted to Sulawesi and even on that island it occurs only in two lakes, namely Towuti and Mahalona.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/mugilogobius_rexi_en/",
      "html": "<p>The water in these lakes is very warm (29°C and more), very clean, slightly alkaline (pH 7.5) and the conductivity is about 225 µS/cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/mugilogobius_rexi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Territorial males become bright yellow and also develop larger fins with dark bands. Females are much paler in coloration and have translucent fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25f-perchlike-fishes-6-gobies/mugilogobius_rexi_en/",
      "html": "<p>Mugilogobius: Latin, means \"mullet-goby\". rexi: dedication name.</p>"
    }
